# Normalize line endings to LF in the repo and on checkout.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` checks the tree out
# as CRLF, and the prettier/prettier ESLint rule then reports one "Delete `␍`"
# error per line (~12k across the repo) on an otherwise untouched clone. Forcing
# LF here means a fresh Windows clone passes `npx eslint src/` with no per-machine
# git config needed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files Git must never newline-convert.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
